  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:4968",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the biological activity of ZR-75-1 through a series of target relationships, all centered on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common intermediary in the pathways of multiple compounds, including Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, which directly targets this subunit. The evidence suggests that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may influence ZR-75-1 through the regulation of the proteasome, a key cellular machinery involved in protein degradation and cellular homeostasis. The presence of multiple compounds that target the same subunit further supports the notion that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may exert its effects via a shared mechanism, potentially modulating proteasome activity to influence ZR-75-1's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the proteasome in mediating the biological effects of this compound, suggesting a possible role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
